/workspace/build-downgrade/README.md:5:This replication package enables the replication of the study "The Classics Never Go Out of Style: An Empirical Study of Downgrades from the Bazel Build Technology", accepted to ICSE2024. The study explores the phenomenon of build system downgrades, i.e., projects that move from a feature-rich modern build tool to a more traditional one (e.g., Bazel to Make). Surprisingly, the paper shows that, in the context of Bazel, downgrades happen regularly—roughly 11.2% of the studied projects that adopted Bazel downgraded to a less feature-rich alternative. The study also characterizes downgrades according to seven emergent themes, analyzed what tools replaced Bazel in the downgrading projects, and studied the generalizability of the themes using a confirmatory context (downgrades from Gradle) and a contradictory context (upgrades to Bazel).
/workspace/build-downgrade/README.md:17:The package includes the code for the artifact and the dataset used in the study. We have provided docker images which will automatically setup various modules of our package (therefore docker is the only dependency). The docker can be easily setup on a Mac or Linux machine by directly applying the commands in the README of the replication package in order. Therefore, there are no particular technology skills assumed by the reviewer. The expected setup time for the docker is a few minutes. Below, we provide more details on the package structure.
/workspace/build-downgrade/README.md:28:   - `current.csv`: holds data related to projects that adopt the Bazel build system. This file can be seen under the `results` folder after running the docker images.
/workspace/build-downgrade/README.md:29:   - `abandoned.csv`: holds data related to projects that abandoned the Bazel build system. This file can be seen under the `results` folder after running the docker images.
